                "On 31 January 1945 the shelling of the castle began, and it destroyed the tower. After the war there were voices calling for the building to be destroyed completely, but in the end only the damaged tower was taken down. From 1948 the castle was the seat of the city authorities (until 1962), from the early 1960s the Palace of Culture, and since the mid-1990s it has housed the Zamek Culture Centre. In 1979 it was entered in the register of monuments.",
