                "In 1828–1869 a polygonal fortress was built. Besides the fort on Winiary Hill, it consisted of fortifications on the right bank of the Warta (Ostrów Tumski, Miasteczko, Piotrowo, Malta, Komandoria and Śródka) and a core on the left bank. In 1902 it was decided to dismantle the core on the left bank, with the exception of the Citadel.",
